WEBVTT

00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:48.310
<b>Episode 1
This Year's First-Years are Hilarious</b>

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:53.000
As part of that,

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:59.260
it is vital that you build the foundations 
for living in a global society,

00:01:59.260 --> 00:02:05.020
by learning from your seniors, studying
together, and supporting one another.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:09.020
<b>49th Kanagawa Public High 
School Entrance Ceremony</b>

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:09.020
So as promising young adults...

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:10.430
Hey, look over there.

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:13.990
I hope you will develop your 
talents here at Kanagawa High.

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:11.320
What at?

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:15.720
The right-hand side of the new students.

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:20.780
Three years may seem long now,
but it passes by in the blink of an eye.

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:18.990
That guy over there is huge.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:24.790
No Outdoor Shoes

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:31.290
<b>Iwashimizu</b>

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:36.130
Anyway, he was diggin' through
the change in the vending machine.

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:37.090
Ha, lame.

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:40.770
Wh-Where the hell d'you think
you're standing?

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:44.040
He's huge!

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:46.200
Are you a first-year?

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:46.850
Yeah.

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:49.760
You're in the damn way!

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:50.810
Sorry.

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:52.110
What?

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:55.820
What's this? His size is all he's got, huh?

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:59.330
This chump's hilarious.

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:00.820
Let's make him run errands for us.

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:02.670
Good idea.

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:11.460
Tch...

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:18.210
<b>Gion</b>

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:20.650
This year's first-years are hilarious.

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:23.430
We've got a cowardly giant,

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:26.640
and now there's <i>this</i> dude
who's as short as a grade schooler.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:32.390
If you know what's good for you, 
you'll listen to your seniors.

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:36.230
You've got to respect the 
pecking order here at Jinko—

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:40.890
Who are you calling <i>short</i>?!

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:43.260
We're already being usurped?!

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:46.600
Let go of him!

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:47.910
You little turdling!

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:53.370
"Little turdling"?

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:56.120
Fine! You're on!

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:58.500
I'll take you all—

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.760
I-Is he...

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:13.300
I'm sorry!

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:17.730
Wh-Who the hell <i>were</i> those two?

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:19.980
That's enough. Put me down!

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:21.990
Let go!

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:24.260
I said let go already!

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:26.910
You stupid freakin' giant!

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:33.540
Why'd you carry me off, jerk?

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:39.290
B-Because they were going to
gang up on you...

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:45.550
B-But thanks for saving me.

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:48.840
I didn't save you.

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:50.580
<b>Shock</b>

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:50.420
I knew it.

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:52.560
I had a feeling you didn't.

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:56.560
I hate it when people call me short.

00:04:56.950 --> 00:05:01.140
And I hate hesitant schmucks like you!

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:03.220
I'm sorry!

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:17.250
I'm Iwashimizu Sumiaki of Class 1-2.

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:21.080
Gion, Class 1-5.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:38.660
Don't follow me!

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:42.020
A-At least give me a break
until we get to the gate...

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:56.210
The volleyball team's over there.

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:57.350
Let's go.

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:02.110
How far do you reckon we'll get 
in this year's preliminaries?

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:05.050
Excuse me.

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:05.050
When you—

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:07.550
<b>Go ahead</b>

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:07.550
<b>Go ahead</b>

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:07.550
Go ahead, go ahead.

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:12.530
When you were carrying me earlier,
I had a thought.

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:20.060
When you're big, you can see 
and do a whole lot more.

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:24.050
Man, it <i>pisses </i>me off!

00:06:25.310 --> 00:06:27.940
What do I have to eat to get as big as you?

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:30.920
How many liters of milk a day do you drink?

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:33.740
W-We mostly drink barley tea at home.

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:35.850
Does that mean I should be 
drinking barley tea, too?

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:39.120
N-No, I think milk would be better.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:41.500
What? Are you making fun of me?

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:48.760
Everyone always mocks me for being short.

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:51.000
They try to sell me clothes 
in children's sizes.

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:51.510
<b>Children's 
Clothes</b>

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:51.510
<b>This should 
be around 
your size</b>

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:53.580
Girls don't like me.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:54.260
<b>Gion, huh?</b>

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:54.260
<b>He's like a
 little brother</b>

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:54.260
<b>Too bad.
His face is
all right</b>

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:57.270
<b>Do you want some 
candy, little boy?</b>

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:57.270
And old men treat me like 
a child for some reason!

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:01.070
They all look down on me 
just because I'm little.

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:06.280
That's why I hate useless 
tree trunks like you.

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:18.580
Iwashimizu!

00:07:19.490 --> 00:07:22.580
Why are you trying to leave?

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:26.110
H-Hachioji-senpai...

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:28.840
Have you grown some more?

00:07:29.450 --> 00:07:32.470
I can't believe you came to Jinko.

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:35.350
I look forward to being friends again.

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:42.920
What the hell do you think you're doing?!

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:45.310
You gave birth!

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:49.200
Sorry, sorry.

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:52.200
I thought Iwashimizu had 
given birth to something.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:53.050
As if that's possible!

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:57.330
Are you a first-year, too?

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:58.420
Tch...

00:08:00.630 --> 00:08:02.210
I'm Gion Kenji.

00:08:03.630 --> 00:08:05.710
Gion-kun... Great timing.

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:09.700
Do you and Iwashimizu want to 
come watch our team practice?

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:14.970
This guy's in a club?

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:18.850
What? You haven't told him, Iwashimizu?

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:22.730
Oh, um...

00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:26.260
Rugby.

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:41.630
So what is "rugby" exactly?

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:43.100
What? You don't even know that?

00:08:44.380 --> 00:08:46.250
A complete beginner, huh?

00:08:47.530 --> 00:08:50.390
Teach him about the game, Iwashimizu.

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:54.640
Don't get the wrong idea!

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:58.490
I only came to watch.
I'm not joining your team.

00:08:59.380 --> 00:09:01.070
That's fine, too.

00:09:01.070 --> 00:09:04.850
But, Gion-kun, rugby's pretty fun.

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:08.550
Once you start playing,
you never get it out of your head.

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:13.510
And anyone can be the star of the team.

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:16.960
"The star"?

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:19.770
Just watch. Okay?

00:09:24.850 --> 00:09:27.620
Hey, Tree Trunk. Explain the rules to me.

00:09:28.090 --> 00:09:29.540
What? Uh....

00:09:30.490 --> 00:09:31.500
Okay.

00:09:34.910 --> 00:09:36.010
What's wrong with that ball?

00:09:36.410 --> 00:09:37.570
It's not even round.

00:09:37.570 --> 00:09:39.850
What? You didn't even know that?

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:42.520
Huh? Something's starting.

00:09:44.220 --> 00:09:48.850
Oh, yeah. Looks like they're 
having a practice game.

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:57.170
Are the rules like soccer?

00:09:57.170 --> 00:10:01.780
Y-Yeah. You have to run the ball past 
the goalposts on either end of the field.

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:08.310
Hey, he just charged into him.
Is that allowed?

00:10:09.320 --> 00:10:11.570
That's the kind of sport rugby is.

00:10:11.570 --> 00:10:14.170
You use your entire body to steal 
the ball from your opponents.

00:10:14.900 --> 00:10:18.320
Big guys like me have an advantage,

00:10:19.580 --> 00:10:23.180
so they tried recruiting me in middle school.

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:27.420
Wow, you're huge!

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:34.440
Huh? It looks fun.

00:10:36.840 --> 00:10:41.410
B-But rugby is a r-really dangerous sport!

00:10:43.250 --> 00:10:47.910
My dad and brother are both man-mountains.

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:50.670
I'm the only small one.

00:10:51.620 --> 00:10:55.170
Whenever we got into fights, I was
the only one who ever got his ass kicked.

00:10:56.630 --> 00:11:03.050
If I could steal the ball from 
a guy that big, I bet it'd feel great.

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:10.190
But everyone's so huge...

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:15.460
If I joined in, I'd probably 
just get in the way.

00:11:20.620 --> 00:11:22.330
That's not true.

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:27.100
Sure, lots of rugby players are big,

00:11:27.640 --> 00:11:30.350
but size isn't everything.

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:32.960
Look closely.

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:38.230
Big guys, small guys,
fat guys, skinny guys...

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:40.010
Everyone's charging into the fray.

00:11:42.020 --> 00:11:45.780
There are no star strikers 
or cleanup hitters here.

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:51.990
Whoever's holding the ball is the star.

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:05.990
Hey, guys. What did you think?

00:12:06.770 --> 00:12:08.990
That was pretty fun.

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:11.460
Really? That's good.

00:12:13.340 --> 00:12:17.260
You're a little small, though. 
You could be a scrum-half.

00:12:17.260 --> 00:12:20.760
Actually, you seem pretty nimble. 
You might be better on the wing.

00:12:21.570 --> 00:12:25.080
Gion-kun, why don't you join the rugby team?

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:30.270
If you're <i>that </i>desperate for me
 to join, I can't really say no.

00:12:32.550 --> 00:12:34.910
I'll knock everyone and 
everything out of my way.

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:38.890
That's encouraging.

00:12:38.890 --> 00:12:41.150
A brash scamp like you should do just fine.

00:12:41.590 --> 00:12:43.000
All right!

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:45.160
Tree Trunk, I need you to teach—

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:49.910
Sorry, but I'm not joining the rugby team.

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:52.410
What? Why not?

00:12:52.980 --> 00:12:55.320
Sorry. Bye.

00:13:03.650 --> 00:13:05.930
<b>SHOCK</b>

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:05.930
<b>Oh, no!</b>

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:05.930
<b>A dead end!!!?</b>

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:12.930
<b>Rugby Team</b>

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:14.480
There's no practice today.

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:17.110
Wh-What?

00:13:17.110 --> 00:13:18.860
We're recruiting today.

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:20.730
Then, what are you doing?

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:22.490
Holding down the fort.

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:26.320
A prospective team member 
might come here directly.

00:13:27.060 --> 00:13:29.660
But I want to play now!

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:32.040
Don't be ridiculous.

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:34.160
Although I applaud your enthusiasm...

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:38.100
I'd appreciate it if you got off the desk.

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:41.590
I'll practice by myself, then!

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:43.450
That's not possible!

00:13:43.450 --> 00:13:44.210
Wait until tomo—

00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:51.220
Sekizan.

00:13:51.770 --> 00:13:53.790
How'd it go?

00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:55.140
Three guys.

00:13:55.140 --> 00:13:56.730
One of them has played before.

00:13:57.130 --> 00:13:58.890
Oh! Impressive.

00:13:58.890 --> 00:14:02.810
I didn't see the towering first-year
you mentioned, though.

00:14:05.350 --> 00:14:08.660
By the way, who's this guy?

00:14:09.130 --> 00:14:10.930
Gion, a first-year.

00:14:10.930 --> 00:14:12.410
He wants to join the team.

00:14:12.890 --> 00:14:14.100
Hm?

00:14:15.990 --> 00:14:18.420
He's pretty small.

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:24.900
For tomorrow's session, once we're 
all done introducing the new players,

00:14:24.900 --> 00:14:27.680
I thought we could do some core work—

00:14:26.070 --> 00:14:27.670
Who...

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:31.470
...are you calling "small"?!

00:14:39.670 --> 00:14:40.720
He's light, too.

00:14:40.720 --> 00:14:43.480
Ow, that hurt!

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:46.190
Don't go around doing stupid things, Gion.

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:50.950
Sekizan's the strongest guy on the team.

00:14:53.860 --> 00:14:56.700
Was that some kind of rugby move?

00:14:57.160 --> 00:14:58.060
"Rugby move"?

00:14:58.060 --> 00:15:01.710
Oh, right. Gion is...

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:06.570
Oh, so you're a total beginner.

00:15:07.170 --> 00:15:08.580
Sorry about that.

00:15:08.580 --> 00:15:10.780
And go sit on a chair.

00:15:10.780 --> 00:15:13.810
It's all right.
It was about 5 percent my fault, too.

00:15:13.810 --> 00:15:15.140
That's not much.

00:15:16.350 --> 00:15:19.730
Oh, that "move" is called 
a tackle, by the way.

00:15:23.630 --> 00:15:25.230
Amazing!

00:15:26.620 --> 00:15:30.070
Teach me, teach me, teach me!

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:35.370
Be polite to your seniors.

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:38.260
Yes, sir...

00:15:40.060 --> 00:15:42.370
<i>Gion's trying to mind his manners.</i>

00:15:45.330 --> 00:15:49.130
By the way, why won't 
Tree Trunk join the rugby team?

00:15:50.750 --> 00:15:52.010
...s-sir?

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:55.570
Oh, you mean, Iwashimizu, don't you?

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:05.020
Literary Club

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:05.020
Calling all bookworms!

00:16:01.460 --> 00:16:02.680
Truth is...

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:07.570
Iwashimizu-kun, what kind 
of books do you read?

00:16:08.600 --> 00:16:11.850
Lately, I've been getting 
into romance novels.

00:16:12.520 --> 00:16:13.410
Nice.

00:16:13.790 --> 00:16:18.890
We were scared of you at first
because you're so huge.

00:16:18.890 --> 00:16:20.910
But now, I feel like we 
have so much in common.

00:16:22.010 --> 00:16:23.670
Really?

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:28.310
G-Gion-kun?

00:16:34.490 --> 00:16:36.200
Come with me.

00:16:40.450 --> 00:16:43.810
What? Uh, um, Gion-kun?

00:16:43.810 --> 00:16:46.460
Um, I have club.

00:16:46.460 --> 00:16:48.500
Just come with me.

00:16:54.850 --> 00:16:56.380
What was he talking about?

00:16:56.380 --> 00:17:00.970
Uh, what are we doing here?

00:16:57.240 --> 00:17:00.600
Where is it? Where is it?

00:17:02.920 --> 00:17:04.060
Is this it?

00:17:04.630 --> 00:17:06.520
No, that's not it.

00:17:06.520 --> 00:17:09.490
Is this it? No.

00:17:09.490 --> 00:17:11.220
G-Gion-kun?

00:17:11.220 --> 00:17:12.410
Man, it stinks in here.

00:17:13.930 --> 00:17:15.090
Here it is.

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:20.350
A tackle bag?

00:17:21.130 --> 00:17:23.600
We can do this here.

00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:28.610
I'm going to knock you off 
your feet with a tackle.

00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:31.150
Wh-What?!

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:35.410
Teach me how to tackle!

00:17:36.050 --> 00:17:37.260
...please.

00:17:38.890 --> 00:17:41.670
Just hurl your body at them.

00:17:41.670 --> 00:17:44.700
Make sure you use
the tackle bag in the shed.

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:47.830
This'll be easy.

00:17:48.350 --> 00:17:51.340
Wh-What? Wh-Why do you want to do this now?

00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:52.880
Shut up!

00:18:04.380 --> 00:18:09.820
<i>Most people are too afraid to charge 
at someone when they first start.</i>

00:18:21.380 --> 00:18:22.330
Don't run.

00:18:24.690 --> 00:18:27.330
You'll get hurt if you do.

00:18:30.430 --> 00:18:31.410
Give me that.

00:18:36.870 --> 00:18:38.300
We're not getting anywhere.

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:40.090
You tackle me.

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:41.930
I-I can't do that.

00:18:42.490 --> 00:18:47.550
We're poles apart in size,
and you're a novice. You'll get hurt.

00:18:47.550 --> 00:18:49.280
I won't run away.

00:18:49.280 --> 00:18:52.760
So I won't get hurt. No matter what.

00:18:56.100 --> 00:18:58.810
What? Are you scared?

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:03.160
I heard about what 
happened in middle school.

00:19:13.560 --> 00:19:17.030
<i>I had a classmate who was 
really good at rugby.</i>

00:19:19.770 --> 00:19:24.350
<i>I started playing because 
he invited me onto the team.</i>

00:19:24.950 --> 00:19:28.620
Okay, let's wrap up with a little game.

00:19:29.400 --> 00:19:31.830
You're really pumped up
 for this, Miyuki-kun.

00:19:34.440 --> 00:19:37.150
Of course I am. I'm the captain.

00:19:38.100 --> 00:19:41.740
After all, if we win the next game,
we're going to Nationals.

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:44.840
Someone stop Iwashimizu!

00:20:03.110 --> 00:20:04.520
Are you okay, Miyuki?

00:20:04.520 --> 00:20:05.760
What's wrong?

00:20:08.770 --> 00:20:09.950
Miyuki!

00:20:09.950 --> 00:20:11.050
Are you okay?

00:20:11.050 --> 00:20:14.170
G-Get a teacher! Someone get a teacher!

00:20:38.740 --> 00:20:39.970
<i>Miyuki-kun...</i>

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:44.900
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:20:51.420 --> 00:20:53.060
Don't be so full of yourself.

00:20:53.390 --> 00:20:57.380
There's no way you'll knock 
my shoulder out of its socket.

00:20:58.220 --> 00:21:01.430
The guy you hurt was just weak.

00:21:04.650 --> 00:21:08.900
Don't insult Miyuki-kun!

00:21:21.540 --> 00:21:25.630
G-Gion-kun...

00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:36.270
Ow!

00:21:39.710 --> 00:21:40.900
That was fun!

